{
  "$comment": "Fingerprints of every sample in test-output/samples/ (written by the BUILT server, scripts/generate-samples.ts). Regenerate deliberately with `npx tsx scripts/verify-samples.ts --update`, and say why in the release notes: a changed hash means existing output changed. Mode `bytes` is a SHA-256 of the file (deterministic artefacts: Ed25519 and RSA PKCS#1 signatures, requests, encodings); mode `tbs` is a SHA-256 of the signed part only (ECDSA and RSA-PSS draw a random per signature, so the signature value can never repeat but what was signed must); mode `semantic` is a SHA-256 of the canonical JSON of the result without its volatile members (evaluatedAt, sha256, sizeBytes, filePath). Each entry's `since` names the release whose output the hash is: it is carried forward untouched while the sample is unchanged, and moves to the release doing the rebaseline when the hash changes, so the chain 1.0.0 -> 1.1.0 -> … stays auditable and every re-anchoring is visible in the diff.",
  "baselineVersion": "1.0.0",
  "provenance": "Initial baseline: every entry is anchored to the release that created it. Replace this note with the account of how the entries were verified; later rebaselines carry it forward.",
